==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Supercat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ironcat''' when obtained from [[Spiky Supercluster (Merciless)|Spiky Supercluster]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Mightycat is an [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]], filling two rare and valuable niches amongst non-[[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha]] units. However, short range coupled with high speed and high knockbacks hinder his usage. Instead of truly combining Wave Shield and weakening, Mightycat seemingly fills two niches separately.

Against [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance]] and some [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave Attack]] enemies, Mightycat truly shines due to a near-instant attack and high movement speed that can cripple targets like [[Dober P.D]], [[Dolphina]] or even bosses like [[Li'l King Dragon Cat (Enemy)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]]. He can be knocked back several times by the same enemy, allowing him to increase the uptime of his already-lengthy weaken. Since the enemy will be dealing half of its damage, Mightycat won't be affected as much by being hit over and over. However, Mightycat is outclassed by [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] when it comes to weakening mid-ranged enemies such as [[R.Ost]], meaning you should not use him as an end-all-be-all anti-Traitless debuffer.

For his Wave Shield role, Mightycat is meant to be used differently than other more traditional [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] units, like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]. His role is to come in quickly and stop extra-dangerous Wave Attacks like [[Axoloty]]'s or the [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]]'s from hitting your cats. On stages with too little space, he might miss his attack because of his speed making him rush into different Traited enemies or fly into enemies with higher range than him. Despite all of this, he is still flexible due to being the only Wave Shield allowed in 4-Crown [[Legend Stages]].

Keep in mind that Mightycat's Wave Shield and high knockback count contradict one another. View Mightycat as a unit that makes Wave enemies easier to deal with, not outright nullified like Octopus Cat against Wave enemies. Attempting to use both of his niches on a mixed stage or against a high-damaging Wave enemy will lead to him being juggled and thus, unable to protect his feline friends from incoming Waves. For example, when fighting [[Kory]], failing to stop his Waves at least means his damage is halved.

==='''True Form'''===
Ironcat's [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]] is intended to improve matchups against a set of noteworthy progression bosses: [[Kappy Jr.]], [[Kappy Kawano]], and [[Master Uril (Enemy)|Master Uril]]. And with the addition of [[Resistant|Resistance]], he functions as a competent counter to them, as the True Form dramatically increases his survivability and lets him utilize each of his hitback thresholds fully. This doesn't just apply to the aforementioned [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] foes either; Resistance greatly improves his performance against all Traitless. He can function as a pseudo-tank who continuously rebounds back onto a Weakened enemy without giving them the opportunity to advance. In an optimal setting, he's steely enough to tank hits up until he recharges. Furthermore, his speed allows him to sneak hits in on enemies like R.Ost and [[Rain D.]] without being turned into a makeshift kickball by their attack rate. As a crowd-controller, Ironcat finally finds his place as a competent anti-Traitless alongside [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]].

Outside of this, Ironcat does little to remedy his performance as a general Wave Shield. Even against many Traitless Wavers like Kory, [[Corrupted Moneko (Enemy)|Corrupted Moneko]], and [[Le'mammoth]], his knockback count is too high to let him tank even a single hit before rebounding. If you intend to use him as a Wave Shield, approach things as you would if he were still Mightycat.

