==Trivia==
*A fan-made drawing awfully similar to this character was entered into the #YourBattleCat contest, with the first form being Supercat and the second form being Supercat & Sidecat.
*Mightycat's name and attire both reference [[wikipedia:Superman|Superman]]. His description specifically references Clark Kent's job at The Daily Planet.
**Ironcat being made of metal likely references Superman's title, "Man of Steel", though his Japanese name, Iron Nyan (アイアンにゃん ''Aian Nyan''), could also be a pun on the Marvel superhero [[wikipedia:Tony Stark (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Iron Man]].
*Mightycat and the [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]] that unlocks him, [[Puffsley's Comet]], both have high speed, many knockbacks, extremely short foreswing and full backswing. Furthermore, both of them can grow larger (Puffsley's Comet in his attack animation, Mightycat in his Evolved Form), and Puffsley's Comet is an [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] like Mightycat's inspiration, Superman, while Mightycat's Evolved Form is an aspiring singer like Puffsley's Comet.
*Supercat's Japanese name, Gi-Nyan (ジャイにゃん ''Jainyan''), is a reference to the ''Doraemon'' character [[wikia:doraemon:Takeshi Gouda|Takeshi "Gian" Gouda]], who also has a large build and aspires to be a singer.
*Ironcat was first introduced in the Apple Arcade-exclusive spin-off ''Let's Go Mightycat!'' under the name Iron Cat before being added to [[The Battle Cats]].
*The symbol on Mightycat's belt is に, pronounced 'ni'. It is the first character in にゃんこ, pronounced 'nyanko', a childish way of saying "cat".
*Mightycat is currently the only [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] and non-[[:Category:Gacha Cats|gacha]] cat to have the Wave Shield ability.
*Mightycat's attack animation is similar to [[Brollow]]'s.
*Mightycat is one of the units to have his descriptions rewritten in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]], as "nullfies Wave Attacks" was changed to "Wave Shield".

